  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Port Orleans Riverside is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want two queens, and maybe a child-size pull-down bed.</strong> The Alligator Bayou "5th Sleeper" rooms officially sleep four adults and add a child-size pull-down bed. In 2026 those rooms ran about $361 to $541 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants a boat to Disney Springs</strong> and a table-service restaurant (Boatwright's) on site.</li>
      <li><strong>People who like the idea of a Royal Guest Room</strong> in Magnolia Bend, at a higher nightly rate than a standard room.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You want a compact resort.</strong> Riverside is larger than French Quarter, and a Standard Location room in Magnolia Bend can mean a walk to the food court and the boat dock. Preferred rooms are closer to the Sassagoula Steamboat Company, dining, shopping and transportation.</li>
      <li><strong>Construction would bother you.</strong> Official pages say guest rooms and select public areas are under refurbishment through mid-2027. Guests may see or hear daytime construction, and alternate paths may be in place.</li>
      <li><strong>Your parks are the main event and you want a Skyliner or monorail.</strong> Theme parks are buses from here.</li>
    </ul>
