  <section id="pools">
    <h2>Pools and things to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ol' Man Island</strong> is the main pool, a 3.5-acre area reached by three wooden bridges. Official pages describe a 95-foot rustic waterslide, a whirlpool spa, a kiddie pool, the Muddy Rivers pool bar, and a campfire and movie on select nights.</li>
      <li><strong>Five leisure pools</strong> are spread through the resort, including pools in Alligator Bayou and Magnolia Bend.</li>
      <li>Official pool pages also say Riverside guests can use Doubloon Lagoon at French Quarter.</li>
      <li>Towels are free at the pools. Hours and lifeguard coverage vary and can change.</li>
    </ul>
