  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Book a Standard Location room if four people is enough and you don't mind walking.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $322 to $483 a night at full price including tax, depending on dates.</li>
      <li><strong>Book a 5th Sleeper room only if you will use the child-size pull-down bed.</strong> In 2026 those rooms ran about $361 to $541. Official listings still cap occupancy at four adults.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay for Preferred if the shorter walk to the food court and the boat dock matters,</strong> or for a Royal Guest Room only if the themed room is the point. In 2026 Preferred rooms ran about $414 to $613, and Royal Guest Rooms ran about $408 to $579.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra adults cost more.</strong> Moderate rates assume two adults. Each extra adult adds $25 a night plus tax, and kids under 18 are free.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Disney's own offers page first.</strong> Disney points to <a href="https://disneyworld.disney.go.com/special-offers/">its special offers page</a> for discounts. Our deals hub will track current ones.</li>
      <li><strong>If construction bothers you, wait until after mid-2027</strong> or look at French Quarter, which did not have a matching room-refurbishment notice when we checked.</li>
      <li><strong>Lightning Lane head start:</strong> Disney resort guests can buy Lightning Lane passes up to 7 days before their stay.</li>
    </ul>
